<h1>Solution 3: The Working Code (MVP)</h1>
<div class="callout">
  <b>Project:</b> CapacityConnect — Digital Capacity Building & Competency Governance Portal<br>
  <b>Required Deliverables:</b> Full-Stack Application Scaffold, Dependency Resolution, Third-Party Integrations (PDF Transcripts, QR Minting, Excel Ingestion), and Frontend-Backend Connectivity.
</div>

<h2>1. MVP Architecture & Scaffolding</h2>
<p>The application is built with a decoupled Single Page Application architecture:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Client (React 18 + Vite):</b> Role-specific dashboards (Admin, Institute, Trainer, Trainee), Exam Arena with anti-cheat proctoring, Competency Passport radar visualization, and QR verification portal.</li>
  <li><b>Server (Node.js + Express):</b> Multi-tenant REST APIs, JWT authentication with role scoping, AI trainer-competency recommendation engine, and Excel roster parser.</li>
  <li><b>Database (MongoDB Atlas):</b> Document persistence with multi-tenant row-level indexing and SHA-256 certificate hashing.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Dependency Resolution Summary</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Layer</th>
      <th>Package</th>
      <th>Version</th>
      <th>Purpose & Resolution Rationale</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Frontend</td>
      <td><code>jspdf</code> & <code>html2canvas</code></td>
      <td>v4.2 / v1.4</td>
      <td>Generates downloadable official transcripts and certificates in vector PDF format directly in the browser.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Frontend</td>
      <td><code>qrcode.react</code></td>
      <td>v3.1.0</td>
      <td>Renders high-density QR verification codes linking directly to public verification endpoints.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Frontend</td>
      <td><code>canvas-confetti</code></td>
      <td>v1.9.3</td>
      <td>Provides celebratory feedback animations upon exam completion and certificate acquisition.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Backend</td>
      <td><code>bcryptjs</code></td>
      <td>v2.4.3</td>
      <td>Pure JS implementation preventing native C++ build failures on Windows while securing user passwords with 10 salt rounds.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Backend</td>
      <td><code>multer</code></td>
      <td>v2.3.0</td>
      <td>Handles streaming file uploads for batch student roster spreadsheet ingestion.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Backend</td>
      <td><code>helmet</code> & <code>cors</code></td>
      <td>v7.1 / v2.8</td>
      <td>Hardens HTTP response headers and prevents unauthorized cross-origin resource access.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Third-Party Integrations & External Data Handling</h2>
<h3>3.1 Dynamic Transcript & Certificate Generation</h3>
<p>The system uses client-side DOM-to-canvas rendering via <code>html2canvas</code> and <code>jsPDF</code> to generate high-resolution, vector-accurate certificates and academic transcripts without server-side headless browser memory costs.</p>

<h3>3.2 Cryptographic QR Minting</h3>
<pre>
const generateCertificateHash = (traineeId, courseId, timestamp) => {
  return crypto
    .createHmac('sha256', process.env.JWT_SECRET)
    .update(`${traineeId}:${courseId}:${timestamp}`)
    .digest('hex');
};
</pre>
<p>Each issued certificate receives a dynamic SHA-256 hash embedded into an SVG QR code pointing to <code>/verify/:certificateNumber</code>.</p>

<h3>3.3 Bulk Excel Student Onboarding</h3>
<p>Admins can upload an Excel (.xlsx) roster. The server parses student rows, checks for existing accounts, generates secure 6-digit access PINs, and creates accounts in a single atomic database batch.</p>

<h2>4. Frontend-to-Backend Connectivity & Security</h2>
<p>Frontend requests are routed through a centralized <code>apiFetch</code> utility in <code>client/src/services/api.js</code>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Automatic Bearer Auth:</b> Automatically injects <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code> into headers.</li>
  <li><b>Session Storage Isolation:</b> Stores active session tokens in <code>sessionStorage</code> so credentials expire as soon as the browser tab is closed.</li>
  <li><b>Proctoring Integration:</b> The Exam Arena monitors <code>visibilitychange</code> and tab switches, sending tamper metrics alongside test submissions.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Quick Execution Guide</h2>
<pre>
# 1. Run Backend Server:
cd server && npm install && npm run dev
# Server active on http://localhost:5000

# 2. Run Frontend Client:
cd client && npm install && npm run dev
# Frontend active on http://localhost:5173
</pre>

